<p>The classic Bear-style traditional grip sits in the low-to-medium range: comfortable, forgiving of cold fingers and easy to find in a hurry. Archers who want a &ldquo;high wrist vs low wrist&rdquo; choice on a traditional bow usually choose by feel. There is no universally best angle, only the one that lets your hand relax.</p>
